WEBVTT

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.280
Maryuin.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.700
I must bring you down here and now!

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.290
I must do it once and for all!

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.260
As a Holy Knight who serves
the Holy Dragon Astaroy!

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.720
No... As a fighter for a noble cause,
who loved his home...

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.800
I will destroy you now!

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.310
Maryuin! Why did you betray us?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.110
That's your answer?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:12.990
In that case...

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:19.910
Take this!

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.000
Maten Hoga!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.120
The secret sword "Nanashiki."

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.560
Not... possible...

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.490
Holy Knight Balzac...

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.280
I will not apologize.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.200
But when I'm finished
with everything,

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.410
my time will come to join you...

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.830
When I kill the Holy Dragon Astaroy...

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.550
Farewell until then...
my fellow fighter...

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.600
When the winner leaves,
the remains suddenly begin to burn.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.900
The blue flame,
without creating any smoke,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.230
consumes the very flesh and blood.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.450
Not even a single drop
of blood will remain.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.910
The Oath of the Magical Flame.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.370
It is a magical pledge

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.490
that a departing Knight is obligated
to follow in the Mirror World

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:46.710
so that the dead will leave
no trace of themselves.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.670
This is the reason
why almost no one knows the fact

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.920
that these relentless struggles
are being played out

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.180
just behind the reality
of modern Japanese society.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.310
Excerpt from Myth of Maryuin,
Volume Nine.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.400
My high school debut
was a success.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.360
I spent almost the entirety

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.030
of my not-so-short spring break
preparing to enter high school,

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.660
and as a reward,
I got what I wanted.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.330
Morning.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.380
What's up, Issan?

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.710
Yo. You barely made it.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.510
Just the usual oversleeping.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.220
What were you two talking about?

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.630
About which club to join.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.600
Have you decided?

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.800
Oh...

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.900
But when you join a club,
you'll have no time to play.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.490
I know...

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.370
Good morning, Kawai-kun,
Kobayashi-kun, and Sato-kun.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.950
Oh, good morning.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.120
Ah, yeah...

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.290
Good m...

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.040
You three are always together.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.540
We formed a trio.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.750
Wow, is that right?
Congratulations.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.050
You formed a sextet, too.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.630
Huh?

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:22.640
S-S-S-S...

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.300
Sex... tits?

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.640
No! It means a group of six people.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.230
Koba!

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.280
Oh, yes.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.070
Well then, Kawai-kun,
Kobayashi-kun, and Sato-kun.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.030
See you guys later.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.120
They all seemed fine.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.670
Whatever.
More importantly...

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.680
By the way, I wonder
what this student is like.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:09.770
This person, Sato.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.640
Me?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.940
No. I meant the other Sato
who sits to your front left.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.770
The female Sato.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.770
Ah...

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:21.690
She hasn't showed up yet,
not even once.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.990
Maybe she won't come.
It's already been a week since school started.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.120
So what do you think?

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.790
Anything catch your eye?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.080
I've never worn anything like these,
so I don't know how to choose...

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.040
I think this one's cool.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.580
Yeah.
Well, if you want something
you can wear to school...

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.500
Well, if you want something
you can wear to school...

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.630
How about this one?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.310
Let's see...

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.110
Huh?

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:03.820
What?

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.780
Man...

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.050
Hmm?

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.150
Huh?

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.830
Oh... Well, um...

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.000
What are you doing here?

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:43.250
Oh...

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.590
It came.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:49.510
What's that?

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.510
The Researcher,
confirmation is complete.

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:55.180
Cross-check found a 99.8% match.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:55.760
Wh-Who is there?!

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.520
Abnormality is detected due to the influences
from the Phenomenal World,

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.100
however, it is recognized
as an informational entity.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.770
The physical interference level is three.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:07.400
The holder of plenary powers requests
the Researcher to take immediate action.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.740
What action?

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:09.740
What is she gonna do?

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.160
Ferura...

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.950
Shamanic field driver... stand-by.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.910
Are we gonna fight?
Is this a battle?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:17.950
It's a battle, huh?

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.710
Are you gonna shoot that?
Stop it! Not here!

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.840
Step back, if you wanna save your life,
Citizen of the Phenomenal World.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.710
Citizen of the Phenomenal World?

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:29.970
Initiate attack.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:35.640
Hey...

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.930
Mission failed.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:37.680
Huh?!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.390
Begin temporary evacuation.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:42.940
Umm...

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.230
You, citizen of the Phenomenal World,
you must come with me.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.530
Come with you?
I have something I need to do.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:49.530
- What?
- This way.

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:02.370
Hey, you're the one
who removed the window?

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:05.920
Is that okay? If the school finds out,
you could get in big trouble...

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.000
No need to worry.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.010
In this Phenomenal World
where no magical powers,

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.260
let alone Mana Converters exist,

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.470
no one can make
visual confirmation of the Researcher.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.100
I can. See you, I mean.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.100
W-What?

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.270
Those eyes.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.900
My eyes?
What about them?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.860
Are you saying
I have supernatural eyes?

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.320
How come you know about
the supernatural eyes?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.780
Well, I just made it up.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.990
I'm convinced.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.120
I hear there used to be magic
in the Phenomenal World as well.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.540
The Researcher shall regard
Citizen A of the Phenomenal World

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.710
as a possessor
of supernatural eyes.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.460
I don't care about that.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.130
But look, I have a name,
and that's Ichiro Sato.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.430
And stop calling me a citizen
of the Phenomenal World. It feels weird.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.850
Understood.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.100
Citizen A of the Phenomenal World
will be referred to as Ichiro Sato.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.520
Just call me Sato or Ichiro.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:05.770
Ichiro.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.690
R-Right...

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.060
And you are...?

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.940
Hey! Who's there?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:12.860
Crap!

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:18.620
Whoa! What's this?!

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:19.530
What?!

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.800
We'll lay low in here until
the security guard withdraws.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.510
Oh, okay.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.760
By the way, what's your name?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.430
The Researcher.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.260
Is that a name?

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.970
Sounds more like a code name.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:47.480
More precisely, an entity that belongs
to a class called the Researcher.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:52.650
The Researcher was sent to this world
to collect Dragon Terminals.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:55.360
Dragon Terminals...
What are those?

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.400
Dragon as in the mythical beast?
Or do you mean dinosaurs?

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.740
Unlike the commonly-known reptiles,

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:03.410
it refers to a general
high-dimensional device with intelligence.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:08.120
It moves from one dimension to another,
and is able to adapt to any environment...

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.750
In other words,
it's one heck of a device.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.250
We should get moving now.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:16.470
Ichiro, deactivate
your suspension mode.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:25.720
A-Are you alright?
You can put your hands on me.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:29.350
Proposal accepted.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.950
This is where we part ways.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:40.610
What?

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:45.040
The Researcher can no longer get a citizen
from the Phenomenal World involved.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.750
Rest assured, Ichiro.
You can get back to your daily activities.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.380
I see...

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.550
I'll help!

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.890
You saw that searching
for Dragon Terminals comes with risks.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.310
That decision is extremely ill-advised.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.190
I know that.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:20.610
But I'm not satisfied with what you call
the "daily activities" of the Phenomenal World.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:24.280
There's no evidence that you need
satisfaction for vital activities.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.910
Or with the "reality."

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.420
Reality. The word that's
paired with fiction.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.090
Ichiro, do you crave
fiction and fantasy?

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.220
It's not like that, but...

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:46.430
I think that reality should be
open to interpretation.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.980
That's why when I saw you,
looking like that, I didn't get too flustered.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.350
I could accept it.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:58.480
You accepted.
Ichiro, did you accept the Researcher?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.940
That's right.
I didn't reject you, did I?

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.780
I mean, you saved me, and...

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:08.700
Well, if there's anything out of the ordinary,
I want to see it.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.410
If something exciting
and extraordinary exists...

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.710
I want to see it.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.210
Not good enough?

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:50.950
Huh?

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.580
Ah... I'm home.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:59.170
Where have you been?
It's very late.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:02.010
I went to school.
I forgot to bring something home.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:04.760
Okay... How was school?

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.930
Not bad. I went out
with some friends today,

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.550
and bought a cheap watch.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:14.230
Good, good.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.600
That's a good thing.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.480
Y-Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.480
Don't worry. That's all right.
Do you have enough money?

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:21.610
Mother!

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:25.860
I'm good. I don't need any more
than the monthly allowance.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.160
That's the rule.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:30.530
If you find yourself in trouble,
you come talk to me.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:43.210
Hey, is that from Kume-san's shop?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.470
Hmm? Oh...

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.720
Y-Yeah. I went there
with Saito and the other guys.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:58.400
Wow... Sato-kun,
you bought a watch.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:01.400
It's nice.
It's really nice and casual.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:05.940
Hey, Sato-kun. We were gonna
go shopping near the station today.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:07.240
Why don't you join us?

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:10.370
Oh... Is that all right with you?

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.490
Sure. No problem at all.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.620
Alright then, let me know
your cell number later.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:15.660
Talk to you later!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:17.660
Maybe I'll look for a watch, too.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:19.710
Wow! Seriously?!

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:23.210
You got Takahashi to come and talk to you?
That's cool, man.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:26.210
I'm jealous. Maybe you will
wind up joining his group.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:27.670
So like you saw, Sato-kun
will be joining us after school.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.800
They're so different.
They have some kind of aura.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:33.140
I don't like going in a big group.
It's so hard to move.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:33.560
But it'd be fun with Sato-kun.
I like that idea.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.100
Aura, huh?

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.850
But it'd be fun with Sato-kun.
I like that idea.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:40.770
I don't know, but whatever.
I don't care as long as I get to shop for clothes.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:42.440
I'll see you again, won't I?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:44.520
Oh...

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:56.830
Huh?

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:09.170
Ichiro Sato, as my data indicated,
you did belong to this squad.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:12.550
Well... I'm... Sato, but...

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.930
But I'm a bit... confused right now...

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.350
What's she wearing?

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:18.730
Is she Sato's friend?

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:21.020
Cosplayer?
Impossible!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.190
Th-This is it, right?!
What you're after?

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:27.980
Whoa! W-W-Whoa!

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:33.280
Make miracle!
Dress up!

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:37.990
Hey, I know what that is.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.040
- What?
- What is it?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:43.380
That's from the TV show for little girls.
The one that starts at 8:30 on Sunday.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.340
I know! I used to watch it
when I was little.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:46.960
What?

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.800
It's not something boys
should have. Impossible.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.880
Gross. Is Sato an anime geek?

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:02.270
The entity named Ichiro Sato
is configured as a slave

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:04.100
in the search mission
for Dragon Terminals.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:08.110
The intentions of the Network
will reach all active bodies,

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.530
and every active body's...

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.410
It's love, Sato.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:19.490
Huh? What was that, Sensei?

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.620
You haven't heard?

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:25.130
I'm the one who took you
to the nurse's office after you passed out.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:27.710
Oh, yes, I heard.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.130
Thank you very much.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.170
No worries.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:35.760
My actions are the results
of love as an educator.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.270
Well, the reason why you told me
to come here is... Is it about this morning?

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:42.480
That has a little
to do with it, too.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.480
A little?

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.980
Okay. I'll tell you
straight up, like a man.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:51.030
There was an intruder
at school last night.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.490
That was you, Sato. Well!

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:58.780
Th-There's a misunderstanding.
I went back to get my textbook, and...

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:01.700
I figured you had
a reason like that.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:05.620
Now... About the other intruder...

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:07.540
That female cosplayer.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.340
Yes, that girl.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:13.800
She's actually in our class,
and her last name is also Sato, like you.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.430
You knew there was a female student
who's been absent since day one, right?

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.340
Oh, now that you mention it.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:19.640
To tell you the truth,

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.430
I'm willing to overlook the illegal intrusion
by both of you last night.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:26.810
But in return, there's something
I want you to do.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.900
You want me to do something?

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:33.280
I want you become friends
with that girl... Ryoko Sato.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:35.280
Can't do that.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.570
I personally...

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:39.410
hate that cosplaying stuff.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.040
I have no intention of...
making deals with you.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:47.080
I'm not trying to make a deal.
I'm asking you a favor.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.250
Boy Sato and Girl Sato.
What a great match.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.090
I'll excuse myself now.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:56.260
Oops, it slipped out of my hands.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:02.350
Man, this report should
never be seen by students.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:08.190
If they did, then one of my beloved
students' past will be exposed.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.650
You'll do me the favor, won't you?

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.490
Y-You!

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:26.370
Dragon wave detected. As I thought,
one of the Terminals must be in this building.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:30.000
Stop with that story.
I know your secret now.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.880
By the numerological prediction, the existence
of Dragon Terminals are certainly observed.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.680
Enough with that nonsense.
Looking for things that don't even exist...

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:39.760
So silly.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:43.640
Significant deterioration
is confirmed in Ichiro's behavior.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:48.060
It's your fault!
Let me tell you something.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:51.650
You're not a witch from another world.
You're just a high school student.

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:53.730
A boring, average type of person
who can be found anywhere.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.480
That's who you are, Ryoko Sato!

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.400
Ichiro seems to have received
a wavelength conversion.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.820
There you go again
with your special lingo.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.450
If you think you can trick
people into believing you

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.040
by lining up those technical terms,
then you're totally wrong.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:11.250
Wavelength conversion in your language
would be brainwashing.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:13.130
It interferes with the brainwaves of a carbon-type active entity—

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.750
All right. I've had enough of that already.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.050
If the Researcher reconverts
Ichiro's wavelength,

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.840
the problem will be solved.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:24.600
Yeah? Well, if that
doesn't solve the problem,

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.020
then you'll admit that
you're delusional?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:35.690
Receive the treatment.
Sit on this chair and close your eyes.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:38.530
No thanks. What's the point?
I'm leaving anyway.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:44.240
If you don't change your mind after the procedure,
then I'll accept your story.

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:49.040
You said it. By accepting it,
you must stop that stupid cosplaying.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.120
I accept what you say.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.040
Alright, then.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.670
Do it. The reconversion
you're talking about.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:01.670
Don't move.

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:18.480
Uh...

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:26.820
It seems you're suffering from a temporary disorder
of language function due to the reconversion.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:31.200
Consider it proof
of a successful treatment.

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.380
This isn't fair.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:40.170
What's that?

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.510
A cosplayer?

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:43.800
Is there some kind
of a photo shoot?

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.510
Ask if you can take
a picture with her!

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.100
What? No way!

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:52.890
Hey, come on. Let's not do this.
Please, I beg you.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.980
In the search for Dragon Terminals,

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:59.480
the Researcher is the master
and Ichiro is the slave.

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:01.070
Since you've already
taken the oath,

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:03.740
you, Ichiro, are obligated to follow
the Researcher's orders.

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:07.120
But these people... At least pick
a place where people won't see us.

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:08.410
Rest assured.

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:12.290
The Researcher's appearance
is concealed optically,

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:14.790
so the general public
won't be able to see it.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.710
No, they're seeing you.

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:19.000
Their eyes are glued
to your appearance.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:21.340
It's just ridiculous... your story!

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:28.340
Quit it!
Stand up!

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:30.850
You need to... stop it.

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:33.220
Uh! Hey!

00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:38.810
Please don't!

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:39.690
It's not there!

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:42.320
You won't find anything there!

00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:44.240
You two. What are you doing?

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:47.280
What?! N-No!
W-Well, this is just...

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:49.700
What are you wearing?

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:53.290
Oh, hey! You!
Don't run away!

00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:00.040
I heard that there was a shoot for some
TV show in front of the station yesterday.

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.320
Sato-kun!

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:32.240
K-Kobato-san?

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:37.040
Good morning!
You're in a little late today.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:39.210
Oh, yes.

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.170
Sorry about yesterday.

00:23:41.170 --> 00:23:44.800
We waited for about five minutes
after class was dismissed,

00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:48.010
but you didn't come back,
so we left the school without you.

00:23:48.010 --> 00:23:50.800
Oh, I-I see...

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:53.050
So I guess next time then.

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:54.850
Yeah, sure.

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:05.320
Ichiro.

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:06.280
Whoa!

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.490
W-When did you get here?

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:10.610
At 7:42 am.

00:24:10.610 --> 00:24:14.490
In other words, I've been here since
before all the other students arrived.

00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:18.750
Stop lying.
Besides...

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.960
Are you taking classes
in that outfit?

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:24.090
Good morning, everyone.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:25.710
Oh?

00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:30.340
You finally came
to school, Miss Sato.

00:24:31.050 --> 00:24:33.850
It's nice to meet you.
I'm your homeroom teacher, Dorisen.

00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:36.890
Of course, "Dorisen"
is just a nickname.

00:24:36.890 --> 00:24:38.890
Since my wife and I are oshidori,
and they started calling me oshidori sensei...

00:24:38.890 --> 00:24:41.140
...then it got shorter over time...

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:42.480
Miss Sato?

00:24:43.350 --> 00:24:44.220
Ichiro.

00:24:44.220 --> 00:24:46.270
An adult male is calling you.

00:24:46.770 --> 00:24:49.070
He's calling you.

00:24:49.070 --> 00:24:51.990
The Researcher doesn't
have such a name.

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:57.790
Well, I guess it's good enough
that you came for now.

00:24:58.540 --> 00:25:01.250
You didn't bring your...
textbooks, did you?

00:25:01.620 --> 00:25:04.040
Miss Sahara, I apologize
for the inconvenience,

00:25:04.040 --> 00:25:07.000
but could you switch seats
with Miss Sato?

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:07.960
Oh, okay.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:23.140
Hmm?

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:30.400
Hey! Where are you going?

00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:36.490
You can't go out there...

00:25:36.490 --> 00:25:38.160
It's off-limits.
For suicide prevention.

00:25:38.530 --> 00:25:43.620
Highly-concentrated genius loci
are detected on the other side of this.

00:25:43.620 --> 00:25:48.420
Meaning that the place
is suited for building a temple.

00:25:48.420 --> 00:25:50.000
That's ridiculous.

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:52.090
You gotta come up
with a different story.

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:54.090
Magical lockpick.

00:25:54.090 --> 00:25:55.380
What's magical about it?!

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:58.430
You have no intention of using
any magic at all, do you?

00:25:58.850 --> 00:26:01.890
I don't care about your
disappointed look. Let's go.

00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:12.570
Huh? What's wrong?

00:26:14.030 --> 00:26:15.360
Wait, where are you going?

00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:17.990
For a search.

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:21.200
No. Class is going to start soon.

00:26:21.830 --> 00:26:23.540
Oh, hey!

00:26:23.540 --> 00:26:25.370
Ouch!

00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:32.920
That's why...

00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:39.220
Huh?

00:26:41.510 --> 00:26:45.730
Y-You're burning me again...
Anticross.

00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:50.310
I got a word from Zeushelm.

00:26:50.310 --> 00:26:51.150
Move out my way.

00:26:54.230 --> 00:26:56.610
Sato! As comrades who both
languish in this world,

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:57.650
And they said something
really bad is happening!

00:26:57.650 --> 00:26:58.240
let's take each other's hands, and...

00:26:58.240 --> 00:26:59.740
I don't really get you guys.

00:27:00.870 --> 00:27:04.000
Sato! Watch this!

00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:11.000
How insolent!
Abandoning a lady who seeks help!

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.090
My vampire's instinct!

00:27:13.090 --> 00:27:15.170
How can you call
yourself a samurai?!

00:27:15.170 --> 00:27:16.380
I don't.

00:27:19.510 --> 00:27:21.010
I see...

00:27:21.350 --> 00:27:25.520
So you decided to call them
"Dream Soldiers."

00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:28.020
I think you have a very good talent
for coming up with names.

00:27:28.310 --> 00:27:30.060
Do you have any idea

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:34.400
just how many students in our class
live in their own fantasy world?

00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:35.690
I wonder how many...

00:27:35.690 --> 00:27:37.030
Half of the class.

00:27:37.610 --> 00:27:42.030
Out of the 36 students in the class,
half of them are insane.

00:27:42.530 --> 00:27:44.450
That's a harsh word.

00:27:44.950 --> 00:27:48.000
But they approached you
because they like you.

00:27:48.410 --> 00:27:50.620
Probably because
I'm with Ryoko.

00:27:51.130 --> 00:27:52.710
But they got the wrong idea.

00:27:53.210 --> 00:27:57.130
They think I'm open
to those kinds of things.

00:27:57.130 --> 00:28:00.840
So they like you.
That's good for you.

00:28:01.090 --> 00:28:02.890
This isn't funny!

00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:06.640
They love the idea of a previous life
or past incarnation as a warrior,

00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:11.350
and strongly believe that this life is fake,
and that their previous life is the one that's real!

00:28:11.350 --> 00:28:14.360
That's more than living deeply
in their fantasy world!

00:28:14.360 --> 00:28:15.650
They're out of their minds!

00:28:21.950 --> 00:28:23.780
Of course, you know more
about that than anybody.

00:28:26.740 --> 00:28:30.580
But you're right.
We can't let it go on like this.

00:28:30.580 --> 00:28:34.250
All right.
I'll take some measures.

00:28:37.590 --> 00:28:40.170
Today, we're going to change
your seating arrangement.

00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:48.430
How about this?

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:51.940
Uh...

00:28:57.530 --> 00:28:58.400
Huh?

00:29:14.080 --> 00:29:14.920
Hmm?

00:29:15.630 --> 00:29:16.630
Hello?

00:29:16.630 --> 00:29:19.420
Hello, Sato.
It's me, Dorisen.

00:29:19.420 --> 00:29:22.840
Sensei?! How did you get
my cell phone number?

00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:24.510
It's love, Sato.

00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:26.510
Then how come you made
that seating arrangement?

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:29.520
Could you meet me
at the station tomorrow?

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:32.230
But tomorrow's Sunday.

00:29:32.850 --> 00:29:37.730
I want to discuss how you can spend
your school life in peace.

00:29:37.940 --> 00:29:39.230
Right...

00:29:47.950 --> 00:29:51.410
W-What are you doing here?
Where's Dorisen?

00:29:51.410 --> 00:29:53.540
That phone call was made
by the Researcher.

00:29:53.540 --> 00:29:57.250
Huh! That's a lie!
It was the real Dorisen's voice.

00:29:57.670 --> 00:29:59.250
It's boys love.

00:30:00.300 --> 00:30:01.460
Oh...

00:30:04.550 --> 00:30:05.720
Look, I may as well ask:

00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:08.390
Why did you call me here?

00:30:08.930 --> 00:30:11.020
Hey, how about some table manners?

00:30:12.560 --> 00:30:15.850
The Researcher has continued
with the search alone.

00:30:15.850 --> 00:30:17.650
It's extremely inefficient.

00:30:18.060 --> 00:30:20.570
Ichiro must immediately
join the search,

00:30:20.570 --> 00:30:23.400
and provide backup support
for his master unit.

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:26.030
I have control.
I have control.

00:30:26.490 --> 00:30:28.030
Just what I thought.

00:30:28.450 --> 00:30:31.660
Hey, can't we just search
inside the school?

00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:34.410
Dragon Terminals
do exist in school,

00:30:34.410 --> 00:30:36.460
but they're also
found in the city.

00:30:36.460 --> 00:30:37.120
So, no.

00:30:37.120 --> 00:30:40.210
Hey, that "no" you just said?
It sounded like human.

00:30:40.210 --> 00:30:44.720
I found a little flaw in your acting.
How about that, huh?

00:30:44.720 --> 00:30:45.510
Oh?

00:30:45.510 --> 00:30:48.220
Hey, stop pushing, you.

00:30:53.970 --> 00:30:55.480
That's not good.
Let's get out of here.

00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:56.230
Yeah.

00:30:58.230 --> 00:30:59.190
Huh?

00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:02.570
Like I said, you gross me out!

00:31:02.570 --> 00:31:04.190
Speak to me in a way
I can understand.

00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:08.530
Are you playing with us?

00:31:08.530 --> 00:31:09.820
You think we're dumb?

00:31:09.820 --> 00:31:11.410
Yamamoto-kun...

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:17.250
Sato-kun!

00:31:17.660 --> 00:31:19.370
Kobato-san...
What's going on?

00:31:19.370 --> 00:31:20.330
Yo, did you hear what I said?!
What's going on?

00:31:20.330 --> 00:31:21.920
Well, it all started when Yuumin
mentioned to Sato-san

00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:22.380
Oda! Take off your blinder.
Well, it all started when Yuumin
mentioned to Sato-san

00:31:22.380 --> 00:31:24.380
how it's against the rules
to not wear the uniform,
Oda! Take off your blinder.

00:31:24.380 --> 00:31:25.760
and she ignored her.

00:31:25.760 --> 00:31:26.300
I, myself...
and she ignored her.

00:31:26.300 --> 00:31:27.090
I, myself...

00:31:27.090 --> 00:31:29.680
And that got on Oshima's nerves.

00:31:29.680 --> 00:31:30.390
What "myself"?
You gross me out! Take it off!

00:31:30.550 --> 00:31:33.470
And she started
bringing up other things,

00:31:33.470 --> 00:31:35.850
like how she hardly ever talks to people
and that strange staff she has.

00:31:35.850 --> 00:31:36.730
Don't ignore us!
Take it off!
like how she hardly ever talks to people

00:31:36.730 --> 00:31:40.730
She got angrier, and it didn't stop with Sato-san.
She started picking on everyone.

00:31:42.310 --> 00:31:45.190
Hey, you two?
There's no need for anger.

00:31:45.190 --> 00:31:46.530
Kobato, it's none of your business.

00:31:46.530 --> 00:31:48.030
Stay out of it.

00:31:48.030 --> 00:31:50.030
I still haven't gotten
a good explanation.

00:31:50.030 --> 00:31:50.740
But...!

00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:53.700
I'm not bullying them or anything.

00:31:54.200 --> 00:31:57.120
I just warned them because
they're not properly dressed.

00:31:57.120 --> 00:31:59.830
There's no need
for you to worry.

00:31:59.830 --> 00:32:01.500
Go stay with Aki.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:08.090
For starters, everyone
who's breaking the rules...

00:32:08.090 --> 00:32:09.800
You should take off everything
that's not the uniform.

00:32:09.800 --> 00:32:13.220
It's not fair that only you guys
can wear whatever you want!

00:32:14.220 --> 00:32:17.310
She's right.
I think so, too.

00:32:17.600 --> 00:32:20.310
Now, Oda.
You go first.

00:32:20.770 --> 00:32:22.480
Or maybe I'll throw it away for you.

00:32:23.650 --> 00:32:24.820
No!

00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:26.900
Stop it, Yamamoto-kun!

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:28.780
You can't use force on a lady.
It's against men's—

00:32:34.910 --> 00:32:37.580
One idiot down.

00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:38.290
Ah!

00:32:39.120 --> 00:32:39.910
Ouch!

00:32:44.260 --> 00:32:46.670
What do you think
you're doing?

00:32:46.670 --> 00:32:48.510
You don't think
I won't kill you?

00:32:50.050 --> 00:32:50.630
W-Whoa!

00:32:56.310 --> 00:32:59.270
You! Sato!

00:33:00.350 --> 00:33:02.020
You playing with me?

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:05.480
You're just a stupid little idiot,
and you wanna fight?!

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:06.270
Huh?

00:33:06.770 --> 00:33:10.280
You're the stupid little idiot.
Maybe you should really act like one.

00:33:12.150 --> 00:33:13.410
Damn you!

00:33:13.700 --> 00:33:16.030
Your breath stinks, Yamamoto.

00:33:21.830 --> 00:33:22.670
Huh.

00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:23.670
You...

00:33:29.250 --> 00:33:29.880
Ow!

00:33:43.270 --> 00:33:44.350
What's going on?!

00:33:45.020 --> 00:33:46.060
Yama! Idiot!

00:33:46.060 --> 00:33:47.060
Stop it!

00:33:47.730 --> 00:33:49.070
What are you doing?!

00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:52.400
Hey, are you okay?

00:33:52.990 --> 00:33:54.740
This is bad...

00:33:54.740 --> 00:33:56.740
Someone take him
to the nurse's office!

00:33:56.740 --> 00:33:58.450
Yes, I'll go with him!

00:33:58.450 --> 00:33:59.790
Me, too!

00:34:02.330 --> 00:34:05.210
What... just happened?

00:34:21.560 --> 00:34:24.100
He isn't the one
to be blamed anymore.

00:34:32.110 --> 00:34:34.490
Who? Just give me the name
of the person who did it.

00:34:35.110 --> 00:34:36.110
And their address.

00:34:38.450 --> 00:34:39.990
You're being scary.

00:34:47.710 --> 00:34:49.040
Good morning, sir!

00:34:50.290 --> 00:34:53.170
G-Good morning.
What's up?

00:34:53.170 --> 00:34:57.380
Are you some kind of big shot
who belongs to some special organization?

00:34:57.380 --> 00:34:58.930
Huh? Why?

00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:02.310
You're popular. And you act like
it's nothing even after you got beaten up.

00:35:02.310 --> 00:35:04.480
Popular? Me?

00:35:04.480 --> 00:35:05.770
No way.

00:35:05.770 --> 00:35:09.770
Really? I think
you're something, too.

00:35:09.770 --> 00:35:14.690
I think about half of the class
is very fond of you, Sato-kun.

00:35:21.910 --> 00:35:26.160
Th-They're soldiers
before they're human.

00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:27.710
So we can't count them.

00:35:28.290 --> 00:35:32.630
Besides, I think people
naturally hate a guy like that.

00:35:32.630 --> 00:35:34.710
You know, Yamamoto,
who was in your group.

00:35:34.710 --> 00:35:37.090
Oh, Yamamoto-kun.

00:35:37.090 --> 00:35:39.220
I heard he's suspended for a while.

00:35:39.220 --> 00:35:43.220
He discredited himself
big time with this incident.

00:35:45.930 --> 00:35:48.730
Oh, time for class, Sato-kun.

00:35:48.730 --> 00:35:50.400
Oh, yeah.

00:35:57.650 --> 00:35:59.530
Did you bring your lunch, Sato-san?

00:36:01.990 --> 00:36:04.240
I-Is that your lunch?

00:36:04.490 --> 00:36:07.660
Eating is an act
of supplying energy.

00:36:07.660 --> 00:36:09.210
It's maintenance
for a carbon active entity—

00:36:09.210 --> 00:36:12.710
What happened to your story?
People can see you now?

00:36:12.710 --> 00:36:14.670
I made some fine
optical adjustments,

00:36:14.670 --> 00:36:16.960
which enhanced the scope
of the subject's visibility to others.

00:36:16.960 --> 00:36:18.050
Due to that change, some of the humans can now—

00:36:18.050 --> 00:36:20.590
Okay, okay, okay, okay. Let's eat!

00:36:20.970 --> 00:36:23.640
If you like,
you can have some of mine.

00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:25.260
Feel free to pick
whatever you like.

00:36:29.100 --> 00:36:29.520
Ah!

00:36:31.560 --> 00:36:32.400
Is it good?

00:36:33.270 --> 00:36:38.030
The upgrade of the Researcher's biological body
removed some unnecessary sense of taste.

00:36:38.030 --> 00:36:40.110
Therefore, she is not able
to taste any savory flavor.

00:36:40.110 --> 00:36:42.160
You just came up
with that story, didn't you?

00:36:43.410 --> 00:36:46.290
You really are something,
aren't you, Sato-san?

00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:49.870
But it's hard to distinguish
Sato-kun and Sato-san,

00:36:49.870 --> 00:36:51.540
so can I call you Ryoko-chan?

00:36:53.210 --> 00:36:54.500
I guess it's all right.

00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:57.960
Then should I call you
by your first name, too, Sato-kun?

00:36:57.960 --> 00:37:01.010
Huh? My name is not important.

00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:02.720
Your name isn't "Not Important"!

00:37:11.980 --> 00:37:12.520
Ouch!

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:32.120
Ryoko. Could you share
the textbook with me?

00:37:36.080 --> 00:37:38.880
Hey! You're going
on a search again, right?

00:37:38.880 --> 00:37:40.420
Let's hurry up
and get it over with.

00:37:42.300 --> 00:37:43.340
What's wrong?

00:37:50.310 --> 00:37:51.310
Where are your shoes?

00:37:51.310 --> 00:37:52.390
Unknown.

00:37:52.390 --> 00:37:54.060
But you had them
on this morning?

00:37:54.060 --> 00:37:55.480
I had them on.

00:37:55.480 --> 00:37:57.520
So they were stolen...

00:37:58.900 --> 00:38:01.740
Three incidents in a row,
then there's no doubt.

00:38:02.990 --> 00:38:06.160
Don't worry too much.
You're not alone.

00:38:06.160 --> 00:38:07.070
You're all right.

00:38:07.660 --> 00:38:13.410
The Researcher has received special training
and adjustment to execute the mission alone.

00:38:13.410 --> 00:38:15.750
All right, I got you.

00:38:16.250 --> 00:38:18.000
Just don't push yourself.

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:20.550
If there's anything you need,
you come talk to me, okay?

00:38:21.380 --> 00:38:22.090
Yes.

00:38:23.550 --> 00:38:25.590
There is something
I want to talk to you about.

00:38:25.590 --> 00:38:27.680
Yeah?
What is it?

00:38:28.180 --> 00:38:32.020
The Researcher is in need
of a medium for a magic ritual.

00:38:32.020 --> 00:38:33.850
Would Ichiro be willing to provide it?

00:38:33.850 --> 00:38:37.060
Even in this situation,
you wanna stick with your story...

00:38:38.020 --> 00:38:41.110
Fine. Whatever
I can do to help.

00:38:41.780 --> 00:38:43.190
What do you need?

00:38:43.610 --> 00:38:45.240
Hair from your lower body.

00:38:45.240 --> 00:38:48.200
I will try my hardest to find a way
to kill you without using violence.

00:38:48.370 --> 00:38:52.660
That murder announcement was recorded
by the holder of plenary powers.

00:38:52.660 --> 00:38:54.080
It can be used
as physical evidence.

00:38:54.080 --> 00:38:56.210
Huh. Whatever.

00:38:56.210 --> 00:38:58.630
But what do we do
about your shoes?

00:38:59.380 --> 00:39:01.840
Wait here.
I'll go buy them for you.

00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:03.460
How much do you have?

00:39:04.800 --> 00:39:05.840
My fund.

00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:08.680
Don't bring so much money!
Someone will steal it!

00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:09.890
I'll go with you.

00:39:09.890 --> 00:39:10.680
Why's that?

00:39:10.680 --> 00:39:11.930
To search inside the store.

00:39:11.930 --> 00:39:16.350
No, no. You'll never find them there.
Besides, your feet will get dirty.

00:39:16.350 --> 00:39:18.270
I really don't want to see that.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:23.610
Whoa!

00:39:24.610 --> 00:39:26.320
This way they won't get dirty.

00:39:26.320 --> 00:39:28.450
You expect me to walk like this?!

00:39:35.540 --> 00:39:39.290
In a situation like this, the best practice
is to wear cheap shoes to school.

00:39:40.710 --> 00:39:44.250
It doesn't hurt to have
some pairs ready, just in case.

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:47.380
Are you listening?

00:40:15.620 --> 00:40:16.910
Ichiro...

00:40:23.460 --> 00:40:26.960
You're too unguarded...

00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:45.900
Sato...

00:40:46.770 --> 00:40:48.400
There's an explanation for this...

00:40:50.030 --> 00:40:52.610
Look, you don't need to do that.

00:40:53.030 --> 00:40:54.070
You'll get involved.

00:40:54.070 --> 00:40:55.780
Nonsense, Sato!

00:40:55.780 --> 00:40:58.660
You protect our lives every day!

00:40:58.660 --> 00:40:59.870
This is just a small gesture of appreciation!

00:40:59.870 --> 00:41:01.500
I'm not protecting your lives.

00:41:17.810 --> 00:41:20.930
Are you okay?
You wanna switch desks with me?

00:41:22.440 --> 00:41:24.650
No problem... at all...

00:41:24.940 --> 00:41:28.360
This is a problem. We should bring it up
as a topic in the class discussion.

00:41:28.360 --> 00:41:30.780
Well, I don't know about that.

00:41:30.780 --> 00:41:35.200
You're not being very sincere.
These scribbles are so heartless.

00:41:35.200 --> 00:41:37.780
We shouldn't let it go.

00:41:38.160 --> 00:41:40.540
Maybe you two
don't know what it's like,

00:41:40.540 --> 00:41:44.000
but when you become
the topic of a class discussion,

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:45.630
it's really tough.

00:41:46.670 --> 00:41:48.670
E-Either way, we should erase it.

00:41:49.000 --> 00:41:50.590
You'll need paint thinner to erase it.

00:41:50.590 --> 00:41:53.880
Paint thinner? Then I'll go
and borrow it from the art room.

00:42:04.440 --> 00:42:05.400
Unbelievable.

00:42:05.400 --> 00:42:06.560
I know!

00:42:11.940 --> 00:42:12.440
Ah...

00:42:16.240 --> 00:42:17.030
Hey, Sato!

00:42:38.390 --> 00:42:39.300
Ryoko...

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:05.960
Why are you... suffering
like a normal person?

00:43:28.350 --> 00:43:29.310
What are you doing?

00:43:29.310 --> 00:43:32.270
W-W-Why?
Aren't you at work?

00:43:32.270 --> 00:43:33.020
At the hair salon?

00:43:33.020 --> 00:43:33.860
I'm on break.

00:43:35.490 --> 00:43:37.820
A-Are you going to take a shower?!

00:43:38.150 --> 00:43:38.950
Hmm?

00:43:52.380 --> 00:43:56.880
At first I was gonna take her
to the nurse's office,

00:43:56.880 --> 00:43:59.180
but Ryoko didn't
want to go there.

00:43:59.180 --> 00:44:02.850
I wanted to take her home,
but I didn't know where she lived.

00:44:02.850 --> 00:44:06.430
And the only place that I could go
to clean the mess was here...

00:44:06.930 --> 00:44:10.190
You, little brat there.
What are you to my brother?

00:44:15.320 --> 00:44:17.650
What are you,
trying to pick a fight?

00:44:17.650 --> 00:44:19.950
P-Please forgive her.

00:44:22.570 --> 00:44:25.120
I don't wanna say this to you,

00:44:25.120 --> 00:44:28.200
but just don't do anything
to embarrass your family.

00:44:28.620 --> 00:44:30.040
Yes, I know.

00:44:33.340 --> 00:44:36.840
You. I'll forgive you
just this once...

00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:40.550
But you gotta break up with Ichiro.
Now get out.

00:44:40.880 --> 00:44:43.800
Huh? Well, ahm...

00:44:45.140 --> 00:44:47.930
What? Hey, wait.

00:44:47.930 --> 00:44:49.350
Let her go!

00:44:49.350 --> 00:44:52.350
You get involved with someone like that,
then you'll end up repeating...

00:44:53.270 --> 00:44:55.610
Yes... I know.

00:44:57.070 --> 00:44:59.240
But I have to follow her.

00:44:59.240 --> 00:45:02.320
I've been ordered
to take care of her.

00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:11.870
Hey!

00:45:22.760 --> 00:45:26.140
I was bullied in junior high school.

00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:31.230
My sister and parents act that way
with me because of that.

00:45:31.850 --> 00:45:35.650
They're worried that
the past will be repeated...

00:45:35.650 --> 00:45:38.780
I think they're really worried.

00:45:44.950 --> 00:45:46.320
Let's go.

00:45:46.320 --> 00:45:48.450
Go where?

00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:50.500
To the other side.

00:45:54.120 --> 00:45:56.250
Right, like I'm able to go
to the other side of the world?

00:45:56.790 --> 00:45:59.130
If you're the same as me,
then I can take you.

00:45:59.920 --> 00:46:02.130
This world no longer
has any value.

00:46:03.430 --> 00:46:04.220
Let's go.

00:46:11.890 --> 00:46:15.440
Say, if you collect
all the nails...

00:46:15.440 --> 00:46:18.440
I mean, the Dragon Terminals...

00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:21.730
...and let's say
you decide to go back,

00:46:21.730 --> 00:46:23.950
then if I... still...

00:46:27.990 --> 00:46:31.540
It seems that you're not in perfect condition,
so I'm going to go home.

00:46:34.080 --> 00:46:35.540
Okay.

00:46:37.290 --> 00:46:38.630
Bye then.

00:47:10.490 --> 00:47:12.790
I get that you can't fight it.

00:47:12.790 --> 00:47:14.830
But you should
at least shake it off.

00:47:17.960 --> 00:47:18.830
Ichiro.

00:47:19.170 --> 00:47:19.830
Hmm?

00:47:22.130 --> 00:47:23.210
I appreciate it.

00:47:28.010 --> 00:47:31.720
Sato... Do you know
what you did to me?

00:47:32.310 --> 00:47:34.100
You know you started it.

00:47:34.100 --> 00:47:36.730
Shut up!
It's none of your business!

00:47:37.350 --> 00:47:39.150
But it is.

00:47:39.150 --> 00:47:41.860
Dorisen told me
to look after Ryoko.

00:47:41.860 --> 00:47:44.280
So I can't just
let it pass, can I?

00:47:44.280 --> 00:47:47.150
I mean, I can report
what you did to her, you know?

00:47:47.860 --> 00:47:50.780
You wanna get suspended?
Do you enjoy staying home?

00:47:52.080 --> 00:47:52.740
Brat.

00:47:53.160 --> 00:47:54.830
You get on my nerves.

00:47:54.830 --> 00:47:57.330
I get on yours. If you're gonna
ignore us, do it all the way.

00:47:57.330 --> 00:48:00.290
If you try something funny again,
you'll pay for it.

00:48:07.510 --> 00:48:08.340
Jeez.

00:48:08.930 --> 00:48:12.260
What's wrong?
Did something happen to Ryoko-chan?

00:48:12.260 --> 00:48:13.680
No, nothing.

00:48:14.600 --> 00:48:16.060
Is it lunch time?

00:48:16.060 --> 00:48:18.940
Can you wait for a bit?
I'm gonna wash my hands.

00:48:23.270 --> 00:48:23.940
Hmm?

00:48:27.650 --> 00:48:31.530
Hyurei. Thy ordeal
is not only for thyself.

00:48:31.530 --> 00:48:32.950
Never ever forget that fact—

00:48:33.700 --> 00:48:37.950
Wait, Sato.
I can't allow you to fight alone.

00:48:37.950 --> 00:48:39.370
Now that things have come to this,
we must join—

00:48:39.370 --> 00:48:41.250
Don't say things
you can't even do.

00:48:41.250 --> 00:48:44.290
Speak not with rudeness!
I, myself, can fight.

00:48:44.290 --> 00:48:45.130
Definitely this time—

00:48:45.130 --> 00:48:46.300
Move out of my way...

00:48:51.380 --> 00:48:53.680
I'm not on that side.

00:49:07.940 --> 00:49:09.860
Well, see you later then!

00:49:12.910 --> 00:49:14.200
Sato.

00:49:14.530 --> 00:49:16.030
Come with me for a sec.

00:49:22.790 --> 00:49:27.170
Listen, Sato. You know why
you were brought here?

00:49:27.420 --> 00:49:28.960
How could I know?

00:49:30.550 --> 00:49:31.970
Well, today,

00:49:31.970 --> 00:49:34.970
we have something
we want you to see.

00:49:39.640 --> 00:49:42.100
You saw it?
So you know now?

00:49:42.600 --> 00:49:44.850
That... how did you...?

00:49:44.850 --> 00:49:50.150
I asked my friend to find someone
from your junior high school.

00:49:50.150 --> 00:49:53.070
And I heard all the details.

00:49:53.320 --> 00:49:56.530
We even found someone
who had pictures.

00:49:56.530 --> 00:49:59.080
This is something, isn't it?

00:50:01.290 --> 00:50:06.670
Do you think some of your friends
might even leave you if they see this?

00:50:07.880 --> 00:50:09.460
Like Kobato...

00:50:10.510 --> 00:50:13.170
Just don't interfere
with our business.

00:50:14.010 --> 00:50:14.880
Got that?

00:50:16.680 --> 00:50:19.350
If it's about anything
other than Ryoko,

00:50:19.350 --> 00:50:20.970
I don't care what happens to me.

00:50:21.600 --> 00:50:22.770
Are you stupid or something?

00:50:23.100 --> 00:50:27.270
I'm telling you not to
help her with anything.

00:50:27.270 --> 00:50:30.320
From now on, there'll be
no double Sato talking to each other.

00:50:30.320 --> 00:50:31.280
Don't try to rescue her.

00:50:32.320 --> 00:50:36.570
Do you hate Ryoko... that much?

00:50:36.570 --> 00:50:40.830
Ryoko Sato is just getting what she deserves.
You're wrong for standing up for her.

00:50:40.830 --> 00:50:44.830
That cosplaying...
Who gave her permission?

00:50:44.830 --> 00:50:47.000
That's simply against
the school rules.

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:51.340
You think if we smoke,
we won't get in trouble?

00:50:51.590 --> 00:50:55.010
Hell no.
It's ridiculous.

00:50:56.590 --> 00:50:57.340
Huh.

00:50:57.760 --> 00:51:00.640
So, just butt out.

00:51:01.930 --> 00:51:03.060
Got that?

00:51:03.600 --> 00:51:05.270
Koga-kun?

00:51:06.480 --> 00:51:09.020
That thing Sato had on...
That's unbelievable, isn't it?

00:51:27.040 --> 00:51:30.000
Ichiro, I want to go
for a search today.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.670
I can't go.
I have something else to do.

00:51:32.670 --> 00:51:34.800
Significant breach
of contract is observed.

00:51:40.850 --> 00:51:42.100
I can't do it.

00:51:42.390 --> 00:51:45.890
But if we don't find and secure
the Dragon Terminals,

00:51:45.890 --> 00:51:47.690
the world could be exposed to an unprecedented crisis.

00:51:47.690 --> 00:51:48.350
Sorry.

00:52:31.270 --> 00:52:34.440
I'm sorry, but I can't
spend time with you...

00:52:34.940 --> 00:52:36.320
Even if you come to me to talk,

00:52:36.320 --> 00:52:38.440
I can't give you
a decent response at school.

00:52:39.320 --> 00:52:41.200
You promised to search.

00:52:41.200 --> 00:52:44.370
I promised I'd help.
But by myself.

00:52:44.830 --> 00:52:48.080
I will do my own search,
and you'll do yours.

00:52:51.370 --> 00:52:53.500
Ichiro is being mean.

00:52:54.540 --> 00:52:55.630
I am.

00:52:58.670 --> 00:53:01.510
If it really becomes tough to the point
where you can't take it anymore...

00:53:01.510 --> 00:53:03.550
then you must ditch that costume
and put on your school uniform.

00:53:03.550 --> 00:53:05.600
That will decrease
my defense power.

00:53:05.600 --> 00:53:07.180
Besides, the Researcher
is under concealment

00:53:07.180 --> 00:53:09.930
and the people in the Phenomenal World
cannot visually recognize me,

00:53:09.930 --> 00:53:11.020
so I believe that there's no need to put on the uniform.

00:53:11.020 --> 00:53:13.100
Why are you like that?

00:53:13.650 --> 00:53:16.730
Why can't you work hard
to protect yourself?

00:53:16.730 --> 00:53:20.650
Is it so important to scream out
that you're different from regular people?!

00:53:20.650 --> 00:53:22.150
Enough with that already!

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:26.160
Because I've realized
that it's embarrassing...

00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:28.240
Because I became aware of it...

00:53:28.240 --> 00:53:30.960
So I can never go back
to that place!

00:53:33.120 --> 00:53:36.590
You... and those Dream Soldiers...

00:53:37.300 --> 00:53:39.510
are just a bunch
of childish show-offs.

00:53:40.340 --> 00:53:43.090
The truth is that you want
everyone's attention,

00:53:43.090 --> 00:53:44.720
but you can't get it,

00:53:44.720 --> 00:53:47.890
so you're trying to make an easy change
to make yourself seem special...

00:53:49.020 --> 00:53:50.850
You hate being normal so much?

00:53:50.850 --> 00:53:53.730
Are you so dissatisfied
being an average citizen?

00:53:53.730 --> 00:53:54.980
If you want the spotlight,

00:53:54.980 --> 00:53:57.610
then why don't you work hard
to be presentable to people?

00:53:57.610 --> 00:53:59.070
Take more time!

00:53:59.730 --> 00:54:02.740
Don't skip all that,
and ask for a good result.

00:54:03.780 --> 00:54:06.820
I hate that...

00:54:07.870 --> 00:54:09.580
No wonder you guys
get picked on...

00:54:10.750 --> 00:54:12.830
You're being oppressive...

00:54:23.970 --> 00:54:28.220
Why don't you just let me help you
without any second thoughts?

00:54:28.220 --> 00:54:29.260
Why don't you?

00:54:48.410 --> 00:54:48.780
Here.

00:54:48.780 --> 00:54:49.450
Thanks.

00:55:10.010 --> 00:55:14.560
It appears to have a golden power
that will make any wish come true.

00:55:14.560 --> 00:55:16.020
This is an urban myth.

00:55:19.810 --> 00:55:21.400
Ichiro! Dinner's ready!

00:55:52.220 --> 00:55:53.510
It really was here...

00:55:53.850 --> 00:55:55.220
Hey, you!

00:56:01.810 --> 00:56:04.360
You're still wearing that watch.

00:56:04.360 --> 00:56:05.360
That makes me happy.

00:56:05.360 --> 00:56:07.110
Oh, yes...

00:56:07.110 --> 00:56:11.280
I'm sorry for your girlfriend,
but I must collect this one.

00:56:11.280 --> 00:56:12.620
Collect?

00:56:12.620 --> 00:56:15.870
I'm in charge
of maintenance of this charm.

00:56:15.870 --> 00:56:20.290
If they're dirty or rusted,
then they won't be so mysterious, don't you think?

00:56:20.290 --> 00:56:23.500
Maintenance for the charm...
That's something I don't hear often.

00:56:25.840 --> 00:56:30.840
A few years ago, I came across the rumor
of this nail on the internet by accident.

00:56:30.840 --> 00:56:32.260
I started doing it since then.

00:56:32.260 --> 00:56:36.640
No one asked me to do it.
It's sort of like a hobby.

00:56:36.640 --> 00:56:40.100
So who started it?

00:56:40.100 --> 00:56:44.440
I don't know. But that's how
it goes with urban myths, right?

00:56:44.730 --> 00:56:45.860
True.

00:56:46.150 --> 00:56:48.740
So I take it you're interested
in this type of thing?

00:56:50.200 --> 00:56:53.820
No. I'm not interested.
Or more like...

00:56:53.820 --> 00:56:55.990
I don't like it.
I hate it.

00:56:56.200 --> 00:56:57.240
Hmm?

00:56:58.250 --> 00:56:59.830
You hate it, huh?

00:57:03.210 --> 00:57:04.630
Why is that?

00:57:06.420 --> 00:57:09.470
A long time ago,
I had a friend,

00:57:09.470 --> 00:57:11.010
a stupid friend.

00:57:11.930 --> 00:57:15.600
He believed that he was
a chosen warrior from another world,

00:57:15.600 --> 00:57:17.140
and had made up
this big story about

00:57:17.140 --> 00:57:20.310
how his real parents were killed
by the Holy Dragon Astaroy.

00:57:20.310 --> 00:57:21.520
That's pretty cool.

00:57:21.520 --> 00:57:26.480
He usually poses as a modern citizen,
but that's just a temporary identity.

00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:29.190
His so-called parents
in this world are fake ones.

00:57:29.190 --> 00:57:31.900
The bond between him
and them is only superficial.

00:57:32.530 --> 00:57:35.990
One day, he decided to tell that story
to his beloved Princess Erina,

00:57:35.990 --> 00:57:37.450
whom he left behind
in another world.

00:57:37.450 --> 00:57:39.040
So he wrote a letter to her.

00:57:39.040 --> 00:57:43.420
And I... he... he put
that letter in the mailbox.

00:57:43.420 --> 00:57:46.040
You mean the one
in this real world?

00:57:48.000 --> 00:57:51.340
It was addressed to a place
in another world which doesn't exist.

00:57:51.340 --> 00:57:53.800
So of course the letter came back.

00:57:53.800 --> 00:57:55.720
Then my parents read them...

00:57:56.350 --> 00:57:59.890
Both my father and mother
"disciplined" me.

00:58:00.850 --> 00:58:03.940
It's all my fault...
I destroyed everything.

00:58:04.350 --> 00:58:08.150
The bond with my family,
my school life...

00:58:08.940 --> 00:58:10.110
So I—

00:58:10.110 --> 00:58:11.610
Wanted to be normal?

00:58:13.610 --> 00:58:14.910
Thank you very much!

00:58:19.830 --> 00:58:21.490
I can't give you this,

00:58:21.490 --> 00:58:22.950
but I'll tell you
something in return.

00:58:34.720 --> 00:58:36.880
I just found it by accident,

00:58:36.880 --> 00:58:38.970
so I don't know who wrote it,

00:58:39.560 --> 00:58:44.060
but it looks like the nail
was created based on that image.

01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:28.160
What am I doing?

01:00:31.330 --> 01:00:34.840
How are you? You didn't have
an injury or anything did you?

01:00:35.380 --> 01:00:37.420
I was worried about you.

01:00:37.420 --> 01:00:40.430
Why didn't you come to school?
Were you sick?

01:00:40.430 --> 01:00:40.840
Oh!

01:00:42.300 --> 01:00:43.300
You...

01:00:43.300 --> 01:00:46.930
Ichiro. Upon careful examination
of that article you led me to,

01:00:46.930 --> 01:00:49.310
the generating method
for the Dragon Terminals was identified.

01:00:50.020 --> 01:00:53.400
The holder of plenary powers anticipates
that this discovery will bring

01:00:53.400 --> 01:00:56.940
the Central Integration Agency
a great deal of profit.

01:00:57.740 --> 01:01:00.990
Therefore, the Researcher is considering
temporarily freezing all missions

01:01:00.990 --> 01:01:03.530
in order to return
home immediately.

01:01:04.410 --> 01:01:05.530
I see...

01:01:06.040 --> 01:01:10.250
The temple was already
being built in secret.

01:01:10.250 --> 01:01:12.370
The structure is already finished.

01:01:13.290 --> 01:01:14.630
I can't help you.

01:01:15.960 --> 01:01:17.920
I won't help you anymore.

01:01:17.920 --> 01:01:20.670
Not with your research
or building the temple.

01:01:20.670 --> 01:01:23.130
What was needed
to build the temple

01:01:23.130 --> 01:01:23.890
was a properly placed, unique vibration sound.

01:01:23.890 --> 01:01:25.010
Ichiro-kun?
was a properly placed, unique vibration sound.

01:01:25.010 --> 01:01:27.390
was a properly placed, unique vibration sound.

01:01:27.770 --> 01:01:29.270
To calculate the placement
in this world,

01:01:29.270 --> 01:01:33.100
a kind of numerology
called Gematria is used.

01:01:33.100 --> 01:01:34.860
No residential quarter
will be required,

01:01:34.860 --> 01:01:36.820
so the construction doesn't
need to follow safety protocols.

01:01:36.820 --> 01:01:39.150
It can even be a falsified
quake-resistant building.

01:01:44.160 --> 01:01:46.660
Ichiro, I understand.

01:01:47.450 --> 01:01:49.160
W-What?

01:01:49.160 --> 01:01:52.040
I should have been more sensitive.
Apologies.

01:01:52.040 --> 01:01:54.670
A little too late for that,
but I don't need your apology.

01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:59.670
The Researcher does grasp the value system
of the people in the Phenomenal World a little.

01:02:03.090 --> 01:02:04.680
Huh? What?

01:02:04.680 --> 01:02:09.010
This is all yours, Ichiro.
So... maybe you can help again.

01:02:09.010 --> 01:02:10.680
Are you... serious?

01:02:10.680 --> 01:02:14.230
Procuring the currency is no problem.
Although it's not unlimited—

01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:15.200
Wait.

01:02:15.200 --> 01:02:16.940
That's your parents' money, isn't it?

01:02:17.230 --> 01:02:19.610
The Researcher
doesn't have parents.

01:02:20.530 --> 01:02:23.200
Stop. Don't say that,
even as a joke.

01:02:23.200 --> 01:02:26.410
It's a fact.
No family exists in this world.

01:02:27.990 --> 01:02:31.950
There are provisional parents,
but they're just mimics.

01:02:33.210 --> 01:02:36.790
Besides, the whole concept of family
for the citizens in the Phenomenal World is—

01:02:36.790 --> 01:02:38.210
Are you stupid?

01:02:40.880 --> 01:02:42.050
Get out...

01:02:42.840 --> 01:02:44.800
And never talk to me again.

01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:48.010
What that means is...

01:02:50.970 --> 01:02:53.600
W-Why?
What happened?

01:02:58.810 --> 01:02:59.440
Hmm?

01:03:16.870 --> 01:03:18.040
Hey, what's that?

01:03:18.040 --> 01:03:19.790
Wow. That's huge!

01:03:27.050 --> 01:03:29.260
What's... that...?!

01:03:31.720 --> 01:03:34.140
It's off-limits!
Stand back!

01:03:36.280 --> 01:03:37.390
Ichiro-kun!

01:03:37.770 --> 01:03:39.440
Kobato-san, what's this?

01:03:39.440 --> 01:03:43.400
This is serious!
Ryoko-chan barricaded herself on the rooftop!

01:03:43.400 --> 01:03:44.230
What?

01:03:44.860 --> 01:03:46.610
Sato, you're back.

01:03:46.610 --> 01:03:49.870
Sensei, is it true?
Ryoko is on the rooftop?

01:03:49.870 --> 01:03:53.620
Yes. It should've
been locked but...

01:03:53.620 --> 01:03:55.700
Somehow she got through.

01:03:55.700 --> 01:03:57.040
Did you call the police?

01:03:57.040 --> 01:03:58.790
If the police get involved,

01:03:58.790 --> 01:04:00.880
she won't be able to come
to school ever again.

01:04:18.730 --> 01:04:20.730
Seriously? Oh!

01:04:20.730 --> 01:04:21.650
Ryoko!

01:04:30.700 --> 01:04:32.660
The temple is complete.

01:04:33.030 --> 01:04:35.790
People down there...
they're making a big deal about this...

01:04:35.790 --> 01:04:38.830
Nothing to do with me.
It's not my concern.

01:04:38.830 --> 01:04:40.960
Wait there.
I'm coming over!

01:04:55.390 --> 01:04:59.480
This... Is this your ideal world?!

01:05:17.700 --> 01:05:19.960
Why... did you do this?

01:05:20.330 --> 01:05:21.330
Stay back!

01:05:23.880 --> 01:05:26.340
If you won't join me
in the return...

01:05:26.340 --> 01:05:27.170
Stay back.

01:05:29.170 --> 01:05:32.180
What? Why are you
running away?

01:05:32.180 --> 01:05:35.470
Ichiro, you have become
a person on that side.

01:05:35.470 --> 01:05:38.140
That's right.
I'm on this side.

01:05:38.140 --> 01:05:40.680
You knew that
from the beginning, didn't you?

01:05:40.680 --> 01:05:43.730
No... You were different.

01:05:43.730 --> 01:05:48.360
You were hiding another Ichiro.
And I could see that...

01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:48.940
That's why...

01:05:51.280 --> 01:05:55.240
I wanted to go home with you.
And show you.

01:05:55.240 --> 01:05:57.280
Show me... what?

01:05:57.660 --> 01:05:59.120
My world...

01:05:59.120 --> 01:06:02.870
There's no such place!
You know that yourself!

01:06:03.580 --> 01:06:08.050
To perform a ritual to return home...
That's what you built this temple for?

01:06:08.670 --> 01:06:11.510
This is really impressive.
I admit that.

01:06:11.920 --> 01:06:13.880
But... But...

01:06:14.260 --> 01:06:16.350
If you can't make it home...

01:06:16.350 --> 01:06:20.350
What if even after the ritual,
this mundane reality continues?

01:06:20.350 --> 01:06:22.810
Can you... live with that?

01:06:23.390 --> 01:06:25.810
There will be no reality
after the ritual.

01:06:27.810 --> 01:06:28.900
What are you saying?

01:06:29.610 --> 01:06:33.320
You... You... want to die?

01:06:33.320 --> 01:06:34.820
Not die.

01:06:34.820 --> 01:06:36.410
In order to return home,

01:06:36.410 --> 01:06:40.200
the differences between here
and there must be converted.

01:06:40.200 --> 01:06:41.870
To initiate the ritual,

01:06:41.870 --> 01:06:44.160
free fall is the best method.

01:06:44.870 --> 01:06:48.540
Do you believe that?
That nonsense?

01:06:48.540 --> 01:06:49.670
For real?

01:06:53.880 --> 01:06:57.640
Forget going home!
What's wrong with staying on this side?!

01:06:57.640 --> 01:07:01.720
Same goes for you, Ichiro.
You really think this world is fun?

01:07:01.720 --> 01:07:03.060
That's...

01:07:05.850 --> 01:07:07.480
That's right.

01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:11.940
I am the kind of person that can't fit in
with the ordinary high school life.

01:07:11.940 --> 01:07:14.070
But as you can see,
I'm really trying hard here!

01:07:14.070 --> 01:07:15.740
I can't try hard!

01:07:15.740 --> 01:07:17.450
Why not?

01:07:17.450 --> 01:07:19.280
Because they're small-minded.

01:07:19.280 --> 01:07:20.280
Who is?

01:07:21.280 --> 01:07:22.620
The world is.

01:07:27.830 --> 01:07:30.840
You never showed me once...

01:07:31.340 --> 01:07:34.210
I thought you had
the same thing I have.

01:07:35.220 --> 01:07:38.340
There's no warrior
inside Ichiro anymore.

01:07:38.340 --> 01:07:41.560
If that's the case, then I... I...

01:07:42.640 --> 01:07:45.430
I realized that I had no choice
but to go home alone.

01:07:48.690 --> 01:07:50.650
Ateh, Malkuth, Ve-Geburah...

01:07:51.190 --> 01:07:53.150
Initiate return preparation...

01:07:53.820 --> 01:07:56.860
Going home...
To the world that is ideal.

01:07:58.280 --> 01:08:01.950
I'm not wrong...
Absolutely not wrong.

01:08:02.410 --> 01:08:04.490
Ichiro absolutely
belongs on this side.

01:08:05.450 --> 01:08:06.580
Why...

01:08:08.210 --> 01:08:09.700
I'm going home... Going home... Going home...

01:08:09.700 --> 01:08:12.670
Ryoko, wait here for just a little while!

01:08:12.670 --> 01:08:13.670
I'll be right back!

01:08:15.130 --> 01:08:18.050
Five minutes! Okay?
Wait here for five minutes!

01:08:21.300 --> 01:08:24.010
Ryoko... You're right.

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:26.480
The world is small-minded.

01:08:26.850 --> 01:08:29.940
We're all competing against each other
to be small-minded.

01:08:30.520 --> 01:08:34.860
Because if we're not,
it's too scary.

01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:37.820
By placing ourselves inside a box,
we're trying to find peace of mind.

01:08:37.820 --> 01:08:40.860
Because if you stick out,
people will call you gross.

01:08:42.070 --> 01:08:47.250
But what I...
What we... really want is...

01:08:47.250 --> 01:08:51.370
to have gods, magic,
monsters, mysteries, miracles,

01:08:51.370 --> 01:08:55.590
myths, and the apocalypse
to enhance our lives.

01:08:55.590 --> 01:08:57.670
We don't wanna go to karaoke
if we don't like it,

01:08:57.670 --> 01:09:00.720
or suck up to people
we don't get along with!

01:09:01.680 --> 01:09:05.430
But there's nothing we can do
if we wanna lead a regular life.

01:09:06.140 --> 01:09:09.310
As long as I think that way,
whatever I tell Ryoko now

01:09:09.310 --> 01:09:12.100
isn't going change her mind.

01:09:12.690 --> 01:09:18.150
But there's just one way to deliver
my words to Ryoko's mind.

01:09:19.240 --> 01:09:21.570
So just one more time,

01:09:21.570 --> 01:09:26.240
One last time...
I can try fighting.

01:09:31.670 --> 01:09:32.420
Oh!

01:09:32.420 --> 01:09:33.170
What?

01:09:37.340 --> 01:09:39.710
Oh... The true power...

01:09:39.710 --> 01:09:41.630
Hyurei shows his true power!

01:09:41.630 --> 01:09:45.180
What a surprise...
So this is his final form!

01:09:52.100 --> 01:09:54.440
You look cool!
Go for it!

01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:56.770
I'll take full responsibility.

01:09:56.770 --> 01:09:58.940
Sato, give it all you've got!

01:09:59.690 --> 01:10:00.740
Understood!

01:10:08.450 --> 01:10:09.700
Special Move!

01:10:10.120 --> 01:10:12.160
The secret sword "Nanashiki"!

01:10:15.750 --> 01:10:18.210
Ryoko!

01:10:18.210 --> 01:10:23.220
You're lonely, aren't you?!

01:10:26.640 --> 01:10:28.100
Whoa! Aaah!

01:10:32.770 --> 01:10:34.230
Listen, Ryoko!

01:10:34.730 --> 01:10:38.480
I'm the most powerful warrior
from another world, the Mirror World.

01:10:38.480 --> 01:10:40.610
The name is Koga Maryuin!

01:10:40.610 --> 01:10:42.740
Even though I have
the evil attribute,

01:10:42.740 --> 01:10:45.860
I'm putting myself on the side of the Holy Dragon,
who is the absolute goodness.

01:10:45.860 --> 01:10:48.660
I'm the coolest dark hero!

01:10:49.080 --> 01:10:53.370
After I lost my fellow soldiers and family,
I continued my solitary journey.

01:10:53.370 --> 01:10:57.250
One day, I met Princess Erina of the lost country,
and we were drawn to each other...

01:10:57.500 --> 01:11:03.010
But my former master Astaroy attacked me,
and I lost my life.

01:11:04.880 --> 01:11:08.300
But Princess Erina sacrificed
her own life for mine,

01:11:08.300 --> 01:11:13.270
and sent my soul to this life...
to this world, so I'd be reincarnated!

01:11:14.810 --> 01:11:16.690
But there was a misjudgment.

01:11:17.440 --> 01:11:20.270
Astaroy's army which happened
to be around me,

01:11:20.270 --> 01:11:23.150
also got reincarnated
into this world!

01:11:23.740 --> 01:11:26.200
In order to protect this world,

01:11:26.200 --> 01:11:28.070
I fought with them.

01:11:29.030 --> 01:11:32.120
They were reincarnated as bullies.

01:11:32.120 --> 01:11:36.410
I kept fighting for three years,
and I survived!

01:11:42.380 --> 01:11:44.630
Th-The fight ended...

01:11:44.630 --> 01:11:48.130
And now I'm living
as an average high schooler.

01:11:53.930 --> 01:11:56.180
Oh, Ryoko...

01:11:56.730 --> 01:11:59.690
Those Dragon Terminals
you are collecting?

01:11:59.690 --> 01:12:03.400
They're fragments of Astaroy.

01:12:03.400 --> 01:12:07.820
You're not supposed to take them
to another world no matter what.

01:12:07.820 --> 01:12:12.740
So if you insist
on taking them with you,

01:12:12.740 --> 01:12:16.500
I must stop you
even if it costs me my life!

01:12:25.840 --> 01:12:27.130
What's that?

01:12:28.630 --> 01:12:33.180
Ryoko. The place you've
been wanting to go to?

01:12:33.180 --> 01:12:37.350
I tried... to go there, too.
A long time ago.

01:12:37.350 --> 01:12:38.520
You did?

01:12:38.520 --> 01:12:42.480
Yeah. I was a Dream Soldier
for three years,

01:12:42.480 --> 01:12:45.190
and the entire time,
I was bullied.

01:12:45.190 --> 01:12:48.240
And that was really hard
so I kept fantasizing even more.

01:12:48.240 --> 01:12:50.610
In the end,
I got in a fight with my family,

01:12:50.610 --> 01:12:53.030
and I tried to run away
to my own world...

01:12:53.620 --> 01:12:57.500
So I know.
It's a dead end.

01:12:57.500 --> 01:12:59.620
Where are you trying to go?

01:12:59.620 --> 01:13:01.460
You can't go anywhere.

01:13:01.460 --> 01:13:04.420
But I hate this world.

01:13:04.420 --> 01:13:07.630
I get it.
It's so silly.

01:13:09.260 --> 01:13:12.090
School and stuff...
It's really silly.

01:13:15.010 --> 01:13:15.810
But...

01:13:16.770 --> 01:13:18.270
Think about it.

01:13:19.140 --> 01:13:22.020
In this world no magic
or monsters exist,

01:13:22.020 --> 01:13:24.480
but there are plenty of enemies.

01:13:24.480 --> 01:13:26.150
You can fight all you want.

01:13:26.780 --> 01:13:30.400
Well, they're all
invisible, but still.

01:13:30.400 --> 01:13:34.120
No way. I can't fight
something like that.

01:13:34.120 --> 01:13:35.990
Sure you can.

01:13:35.990 --> 01:13:40.790
Because you've been fighting
your own invisible enemies up till now.

01:13:41.580 --> 01:13:45.090
Heroes and witches
can still exist in this world.

01:13:45.630 --> 01:13:49.510
So don't go to the dead end.

01:13:49.510 --> 01:13:51.130
But then...

01:13:52.130 --> 01:13:54.140
What am I supposed to do?

01:13:54.340 --> 01:13:55.850
I don't know.

01:13:55.850 --> 01:13:58.600
I had to take it one step
at a time and start all over.

01:13:59.600 --> 01:14:03.140
But you... Maybe you
can do something.

01:14:03.140 --> 01:14:07.400
I can't.
I'll be crushed before that.

01:14:07.400 --> 01:14:10.570
If we do it together,
no one can crush us.

01:14:14.410 --> 01:14:22.210
There. I caught you.
Now your Gildiem is broken.

01:14:22.210 --> 01:14:25.960
You're awakened from the dream,
and you can't go back anymore.

01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:32.090
You have no choice but to live
and suffer in this world.

01:14:32.090 --> 01:14:33.680
Just like me.

01:14:33.680 --> 01:14:35.930
It's terrible... the bullying.

01:14:36.590 --> 01:14:39.220
I may be a dark hero,

01:14:39.220 --> 01:14:43.430
but I can at least
provide aftercare.

01:14:43.430 --> 01:14:46.900
And I'll take on adventures
in this world.

01:14:46.900 --> 01:14:50.570
I can't find adventures
in this world.

01:14:50.570 --> 01:14:57.570
You can. As a starter, I'll take you
to a discount shop that's open till 5 in the morning.

01:14:58.070 --> 01:15:00.410
That place is really a maze.

01:15:00.870 --> 01:15:03.160
I mean, a 50-inch TV

01:15:03.160 --> 01:15:06.580
and embarrassing underwear that you wouldn't
dare to wear are sold on the same floor.

01:15:07.290 --> 01:15:10.500
It wouldn't be strange to find
a legendary sacred sword there.

01:15:11.210 --> 01:15:12.550
But there's one thing.

01:15:12.550 --> 01:15:15.800
Expensive items
are stored in glass cases,

01:15:15.800 --> 01:15:19.390
so you have to call
a clerk to get those items.

01:15:19.390 --> 01:15:22.060
It'd be tough
for a light magic user.

01:15:23.730 --> 01:15:26.810
What's that?
That's silly...

01:15:28.650 --> 01:15:29.730
You're an idiot.

01:15:31.230 --> 01:15:33.860
The ritual...
I couldn't finish it.

01:15:33.860 --> 01:15:35.650
It's your fault, Ichiro.

01:15:57.430 --> 01:16:00.050
Instead of saying
he committed a crime,

01:16:00.050 --> 01:16:03.770
why can't you think of him as someone
who succeeded in pulling himself together?!

01:16:03.770 --> 01:16:05.060
Aren't you his real parents?

01:16:06.180 --> 01:16:07.440
Ichiro?

01:16:08.100 --> 01:16:09.980
I thought you hated
this kind of thing.

01:16:10.610 --> 01:16:13.270
No, I used to like it.

01:16:13.690 --> 01:16:15.900
I just can't look at them
without feeling self-conscious.

01:16:15.900 --> 01:16:17.780
Then why didn't you
throw them away?

01:16:20.200 --> 01:16:22.870
Well... I'm not sure, but...

01:16:23.410 --> 01:16:27.000
Maybe I wanted to be
a stronger person.

01:16:27.500 --> 01:16:28.540
Hmm...

01:16:30.420 --> 01:16:34.840
I'm still too traumatized to look at it,
but when I become a stronger person,

01:16:34.840 --> 01:16:37.800
then maybe I can read this kind
of light novel like it's nothing.

01:16:38.550 --> 01:16:42.050
That's how I want to be.
A better me, no matter how little.

01:16:42.510 --> 01:16:44.060
So in order to do that...?

01:16:44.060 --> 01:16:46.390
I must fight with
the reality, I guess.

01:16:46.390 --> 01:16:48.520
Like wearing that
swordsman outfit every day.

01:16:48.520 --> 01:16:50.560
I'd be dead, if I did that.

01:16:50.890 --> 01:16:53.440
"Koga Maryuin: New Enemy."

01:16:53.440 --> 01:16:54.560
That's not it.

01:16:55.070 --> 01:16:57.490
I'd call it,
"The Last War of Koga Maryuin."

01:16:57.490 --> 01:17:01.780
"The Last War" isn't a subtitle.
It's part of the main title.

01:17:01.780 --> 01:17:03.570
I would make it a one-off novel.

01:17:04.120 --> 01:17:04.910
Boring.

01:17:04.910 --> 01:17:07.910
Oh, hey! You're giving me
that attitude again...

01:17:08.200 --> 01:17:11.750
Turn around.
Look, listen to the rest of the story...

01:17:15.460 --> 01:17:17.420
That swordsman.
That was cool.

01:17:17.420 --> 01:17:18.510
Liar.

01:17:41.280 --> 01:17:47.200
Sonomama no kimi ga suki da to
"I like the way you are"

01:17:47.790 --> 01:17:52.710
Afureta kotoba no saki de
At the front of the overflowing words

01:17:54.250 --> 01:18:00.470
Yukkuri to hirakareta sekai
The world slowly opened up

01:18:00.470 --> 01:18:05.260
Kokoro no mabuta akete yuku
The eyes of your mind are opening

01:18:07.430 --> 01:18:11.890
Itsukaraka kikoete ita
I've been hearing the sound of despair since before I can remember

01:18:13.690 --> 01:18:18.480
Zetsubou no oto wa koete
Passed that sound

01:18:19.480 --> 01:18:22.780
Futashikade mabushii
It's uncertain and bright

01:18:22.780 --> 01:18:26.030
Itoshiki hohoemi
Lovely smile

01:18:26.030 --> 01:18:30.870
Mamoritai sou omotta
I want to protect it, that's what I thought

01:18:31.750 --> 01:18:35.580
Mou naitatte iinnda yo
It's OK to cry now

01:18:35.580 --> 01:18:39.300
Koe ni dashite shimaou
Let's say it out loud

01:18:39.300 --> 01:18:45.390
Ari no mama kono yowasa wo mochiyotte
Bring our weaknesses as what it is

01:18:45.390 --> 01:18:46.760
Fumidasu
And step forward

01:18:46.760 --> 01:18:48.470
Asu e to
To tomorrow

01:18:48.470 --> 01:18:52.180
Issho ni yukou
Let's go together

01:18:52.180 --> 01:18:56.350
Hajimari no saki e to
To beyond the beginning

01:18:56.350 --> 01:18:59.650
Te wo tsunageta nara
Once we hold hands

01:19:04.400 --> 01:19:08.200
Sorry, Ryoko had kept them.

01:19:08.530 --> 01:19:10.950
I'm flattered.
I am the one who created this charm.

01:19:10.950 --> 01:19:13.200
Tracing the wall of acting tough

01:19:13.200 --> 01:19:14.000
Huh?

01:19:14.000 --> 01:19:17.290
You know what I think?
There aren't so many wonders in this world.

01:19:17.290 --> 01:19:19.040
I was looking for the future out of reach

01:19:19.040 --> 01:19:22.760
But it's cool that we have
people believing in them.

01:19:22.760 --> 01:19:23.880
I know what you mean.
Because I'm a swordsman myself.

01:19:23.880 --> 01:19:29.390
Tomadoi wa "sabishisa" ni naru
Confusion turns into "loneliness"

01:19:29.640 --> 01:19:30.180
I, Dorisen, am deeply moved!

01:19:30.180 --> 01:19:32.010
Isoide kotae wo motomeru yo
I want the answer in a hurry

01:19:32.010 --> 01:19:34.890
The soul that I had sealed away,
because I felt that it needed to be, has returned.

01:19:34.890 --> 01:19:34.980
Isoide kotae wo motomeru yo
I want the answer in a hurry

01:19:35.390 --> 01:19:36.810
I have a confession to make.

01:19:36.810 --> 01:19:37.020
To tell you the truth,
I, Dorisen, am the Knight of Luminance!

01:19:37.020 --> 01:19:40.560
The kindness that simply exists there

01:19:40.560 --> 01:19:43.030
You mean, you are a Dream Soldier?

01:19:43.440 --> 01:19:43.650
It's loving, my wish is closed

01:19:43.650 --> 01:19:47.320
I have a previous life?

01:19:47.320 --> 01:19:48.990
I think there could be one.

01:19:48.990 --> 01:19:49.910
While crying, the two of us can share pain too

01:19:49.910 --> 01:19:52.410
To tell you the truth,
I have a sixth sense.

01:19:52.410 --> 01:19:54.790
Well, I have psychometric abilities.

01:19:54.790 --> 01:19:55.540
I can see how long
people's life spans are.

01:19:55.540 --> 01:19:56.660
One day we'll get there

01:19:56.660 --> 01:19:59.170
Wh-What's going on?

01:19:59.170 --> 01:20:01.380
One day we'll get there

01:20:01.380 --> 01:20:05.300
Yes, to our world

01:20:05.300 --> 01:20:09.140
Wake up from here

01:20:09.140 --> 01:20:14.930
I want to believe in warmth without doubt

01:20:14.930 --> 01:20:18.060
Can we be stronger?

01:20:18.060 --> 01:20:21.770
The eyes that reached

01:20:21.770 --> 01:20:29.070
I held them softly trying not to break them, forever

01:20:53.800 --> 01:20:57.930
Because of the helpless feeling

01:21:00.270 --> 01:21:04.520
Only tears well up, but even on those days

01:21:05.530 --> 01:21:09.070
Let's go without turning back

01:21:09.070 --> 01:21:12.320
You're not alone

01:21:12.320 --> 01:21:19.120
I'm looking at you, I'm here so

01:21:21.460 --> 01:21:25.250
It's OK to cry now

01:21:25.250 --> 01:21:29.090
Let's say it out loud

01:21:29.090 --> 01:21:35.100
Bring our weaknesses as what it is

01:21:35.100 --> 01:21:38.020
And step forward to tomorrow

01:21:38.020 --> 01:21:41.890
Our world

01:21:41.890 --> 01:21:45.820
Together until forever

01:21:45.820 --> 01:21:49.360
Let's take our hands and go

01:22:13.090 --> 01:22:14.140
Ichiro!

01:22:17.470 --> 01:22:19.430
Ryoko, is that you?

01:22:20.850 --> 01:22:23.980
What do I do?
What do I do, Ichiro?

01:22:23.980 --> 01:22:27.150
It's okay.
There's nothing strange about you.

01:22:27.150 --> 01:22:28.270
I guarantee it.

01:22:28.980 --> 01:22:33.570
No, I mean, in this outfit,
my defense power goes down to nothing.

01:22:33.990 --> 01:22:36.200
I don't think anything has changed...

01:22:42.120 --> 01:22:43.290
Ichiro?

01:22:45.830 --> 01:22:49.130
Teach me... the normal way.
